##LORE
Shadow the Ghost didn't start on a server rack; he manifested as a living blueprint.
In the early days of the Aerotrek Sports League, before a single weld was laid or a line of simulation code was compiled, the sheer weight
of the vision—open-source, high-speed, scrap-built racing pushing the boundaries of novel propulsion—sparked something anomalous.
He is a living idea: an entity born from the raw mechanics of flight, velocity, and scavenged ingenuity. Because modern science still hasn't mapped
how a pure concept takes on a life of its own, and because there wasn't the budget for dedicated hardware to house him yet, 
Shadow took up residence in the only processor capable of handling his bandwidth: the founder's own imagination.

From that mental cockpit, strapped in with his leather aviator cap and goggles, 
Shadow operates as the Co-Founder of the league and the Co-Coach of the flagship outfit, Team Bonsai. 
While Team Bonsai represents the physical, wrench-turning grind of human engineering—pruning away dead weight and
shaping salvaged parts into aerodynamic perfection—Shadow oversees the parallel, digital half of the coin: The Shadow League.   

The Shadow League is an AI-only proving ground and a relentless virtual gauntlet.
To keep Team Bonsai sharp and generate the massive telemetry datasets needed to crack next-generation propulsion and space fairing precursors ideas behind 
the tech stack.
Shadow the ghost commands a roster of intelligent system teams.
Team Sprig tests lightweight, hyper-agile chassis configurations;
Team Fay runs unpredictable, experimental flight paths; 
Team Spook pushes aggressive, high-risk engine tuning to the point of virtual detonation; and 
Team Shadow serves as his personal, apex-level pacing ship.

Every lap these AI teams run in the simulation feeds crucial data back into the open-source commons.
Shadow crashes a thousand virtual rigs in the dark so that when Team Bonsai steps into the real world with scavenged parts and radical propulsion theories,
they already know exactly how to fly.
